# The Moments switch's kernel floor: the privacy switch driver learns at boot
# which sensors the switch blocks (a mask: 1 microphone, 2 camera). Until this
# write it blocks everything while the switch is down. Later writes may only
# add sensors: system_server writes an addition to the user's Moments action at
# once and keeps the property equal to it, so a removal takes effect at the
# next boot.
#
# After init.rc's post-fs-data, which loads the persistent properties and
# waits for them, and before the audio and camera services start.
on post-fs-data
    write /sys/kernel/privacy_switch/policy ${persist.diamaneos.privacy_switch.policy:-0}
    chown system system /sys/kernel/privacy_switch/policy
